about arithmetic operators. Here is the
first point. Result of division is

95
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:20.000
floating point if either or both the
operants are floating point.

96
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:26.000
Always remember this. If one of the
operants or both the operants are

97
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.000
floating point values, then the result
of division will also be a floatingoint

98
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:40.000
value. For example, in this specific
case, I have this expression 12 / 5.0.

99
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.000
Here we have this floating point value
as the operand. Clearly, we will get the

100
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:51.000
result as 2.4. We are getting a floating
point value here. If we have 12.0 0 in

101
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:57.000
place of 12 and five in place of 5.0
then also we''ll get the same result. If

102
