h operation is equal to symbol is double equals sign. We have double equal as the symbol for is equal to. Example is 3= 6. We know 3 is not equal to 6. So we will get zero as the result. Now here is the last operation. The sixth operation which is not equal to symbol for not equal to is exclamation mark with equal symbol. And here is the example 3 not= 6. Here I''m checking whether 3 is not equal to 6. We know 3 is not equal to 6. So we will get one as the result. I hope these operators are clear to you. These are all the relational operators we have in C++. So with this we have understood what are relational operators. What are the different types of relational operators we have and with the help of these examples we have understood how these relational operators work. So with this we have understood the topic relational operators and this means we are done with this lecture. Okay friends this is it for now. Thank you for watching this lecture. I will see you in the next one. [Applause] [Music]', '[{"start": 0.0, "end": 3.0, "text": "Hello everyone, welcome to Nesso"}, {"start": 3.0, "end": 5.0, "text": "Academy. In the previous lecture, we"}, {"start": 5.0, "end": 9.0, "text": "understood conditional operator in C++."}, {"start": 9.0, "end": 12.0, "text": "We learned that conditional operator is"}, {"start": 12.0, "end": 15.0, "text": "a turnary operator because it accepts"}, {"start": 15.0, "end": 17.0, "text": "three operants."}, {"start": 17.0, "end": 20.0, "text": "Now in this lecture we will understand"}, {"start": 20.0, "end": 23.0, "text": "relational operators. The focus of this"}, {"start": 23.0, "end": 25.0, "text": "lecture is to properly understand"}, {"start": 25.0, "end": 29.0, "text": "relational operators in C++."}, {"start": 29.0, "end": 32.0, "text": "So without any further delay, let''s get"}, {"start": 32.0, "end": 34.0, "text": "started with this lecture and let''s see"}, {"start": 34.0, "end": 37.0, "text": "what are the topics."}, {"start": 