": "This is the local variable. Now, why am\nI calling this a local variable?"}, {"start": 426.0, "end": 432.0, "text": "This is because this variable is defined\nwithin the main function."}, {"start": 432.0, "end": 438.0, "text": "This variable has the scope of the main\nfunction and therefore this variable is"}, {"start": 438.0, "end": 443.0, "text": "accessible within this main function\nonly. Whenever we define a variable"}, {"start": 443.0, "end": 449.0, "text": "within a function that variable is\ncalled a local variable."}, {"start": 449.0, "end": 454.0, "text": "So this variable is local to this\nfunction. It has the scope of this"}, {"start": 454.0, "end": 459.0, "text": "function.\nNow you can observe that the name of the"}, {"start": 459.0, "end": 464.0, "text": "global variable and the name of the\nlocal variable is same. So now the"}, {"start": 464.0, "end": 471.0, "text": "question arises that if we try to access\nx in our main function then which"}, {"start": 471.0, "end": 478.0, "text": "variable will be accessed will it be a\nglobal variable or a local variable?"}, {"start": 478.0, "end": 485.0, "text": "Here in this std see out statement I am\ntrying to access the value of x. I have"}, {"start": 485.0, "end": 492.0, "text": "specified X here. Now my question is\nwill this value will be accessed or this"}, {"start": 492.0, "end": 497.0, "text": "value will be accessed. There is a clash\nbetween these two variables. These"}, {"start": 497.0, "end": 503.0, "text": "variables have the same name.\nWhich variable will be accessed? Will it"}, {"start": 503.0, "end": 506.0, "text": "be a global variable or a local\nvariable?"}, {"start": 506.0, "end": 512.0, "text": "The answer to this question is the local\nvariable will be accessed because the"}, {"start": 512.0, "end": 519.0, "text": "local variable takes priority over the\nglobal variable. It is always the case."}, {"start": 519.0, "end": 525.0, "text": "Whenever there is such clash always the\nlocal variable wins. Here I have"}, {"start": 525.0, "end": 531.0, "text": "specified the name X. So clearly we will\nget value five here because the local"}, {"start": 531.0, "end": 537.0, "text": "variable wins over the global variable.\nSo now we know the value of the local"}, {"start": 537.0, "end": 543.0, "text": "variable X will be displayed by this std\nseeout statement. I hope this is clear"}, {"start": 543.0, "end": 549.0, "text": "to you. Now let''s say we want to access\nthis global variable X. Then how do we"}, {"start": 549.0, "end": 554.0, "text": "access this variable? We know that this\nlocal variable is hiding this global"}, {"start": 554.0, "end": 560.0, "text": "variable. Whenever we specify X, the\nlocal variable wins over the global"}, {"start": 560.0, "end": 565.0, "text": "variable. Now the question is how do we\naccess this global variable?"}, {"start": 565.0, "end": 571.0, "text": "We can access this global variable with\nthe help of the scope resolution"}, {"start": 571.0, "end": 577.0, "text": "operator. Here I have done this job.\nHere we have this stdcout statement and"}, {"start": 577.0, "end": 582.0, "text": "here I have specified the scope\nresolution operator along with the"}, {"start": 582.0, "end": 588.0, "text": "variable x.\nHere I''m trying to access the global"}, {"start": 588.0, "end": 592.0, "text": "variable X.\nFrom here also it is clear that if a"}, {"start": 592.0, "end": 598.0, "text": "local variable hides a global one, use\nscope resolution operator to access the"}, {"start": 598.0, "end": 604.0, "text": "global variable. Here I''m using the\nscope resolution operator to access this"}, {"start": 604.0, "end": 608.0, "text": "global variable. Here we know we get\nvalue 10."}, {"start": 608.0, "end": 614.0, "text": "So we will get the expected outcome from\nthis program. we''ll get this output"}, {"start": 614.0, "end": 620.0, "text": "local x5 then global x10 first we are\ngetting the value of the local variable"}, {"start": 620.0, "end": 627.0, "text": "that''s what we can see and then we are\ngetting the value of the global variable"}, {"start": 627.0, "end": 631.0, "text": "so that''s the concept of the scope\nresolution operator it allows us to"}, {"start": 631.0, "end": 637.0, "text": "access the global variable if it is\nhidden by the local variable"}, {"start": 637.0, "end": 644.0, "text": "now let''s say if we do not have the\nlocal variable x Then if we specify x we"}, {"start": 644.0, "end": 648.0, "text": "will get the access of the global\nvariable because there is no such local"}, {"start": 648.0, "end": 653.0, "text": "variable available in the function. But\nif we have the local variable which is"}, {"start": 653.0, "end": 659.0, "text": "hiding the global variable then we need\nto use the scope resolution operator to"}, {"start": 659.0, "end": 664.0, "text": "access the global variable. I hope this\nidea is clear to you. So we are done"}, {"start": 664.0, "end": 669.0, "text": "with the first use case. Now let''s move\nto the second use case."}, {"start": 669.0, "end": 674.0, "text": "The second use case is accessing name\nspaces."}, {"start": 674.0, "end": 681.0, "text": "When using names from a name space, use\nscope resolution operator to access the"}, {"start": 681.0, "end": 686.0, "text": "name.\nAs I have mentioned this already, if"}, {"start": 686.0, "end": 693.0, "text": "some name or an entity is defined within\na name space and if we want to access"}, {"start": 693.0, "end": 700.0, "text": "that entity outside the name space then\nwe need to use the scope resolution"}, {"start": 700.0, "end": 704.0, "text": "operator.\nHere is the example to demonstrate the"}, {"start": 704.0, "end": 709.0, "text": "same. I have included the IO stream\nheader file inside this main function"}, {"start": 709.0, "end": 716.0, "text": "with the help of stdc out. I''m trying to\ndisplay hello nesso on the screen. Now"}, {"start": 716.0, "end": 723.0, "text": "here you can observe that std is the\nname of the name space where see out"}, {"start": 723.0, "end": 730.0, "text": "object is available. To access this\nobject outside the std name space that"}, {"start": 730.0, "end": 736.0, "text": "is within this main function we need to\nuse the scope resolution operator like"}, {"start": 736.0, "end": 742.0, "text": "this. So it is following the syntax\nwhich we have already seen. Here"}, {"start": 742.0, "end": 748.0, "text": "we are accessing see out in the std name\nspace through the scope resolution"}, {"start": 748.0, "end": 753.0, "text": "operator. See out object is available in\nthe std name space. We are trying to"}, {"start": 753.0, "end": 760.0, "text": "access it. I hope this is clear to you.\nSo we have been using stdc out without"}, {"start": 760.0, "end": 766.0, "text": "realizing that we have the scope\nresolution operator between the two and"}, {"start": 766.0, "end": 773.0, "text": "this operator is helping us to access\nthis object available in the std name"}, {"start": 773.0, "end": 776.0, "text": "space.\nWe know the syntax is correct. We will"}, {"start": 776.0, "end": 782.0, "text": "get the correct output. We will get\nhello nesso as the output. So with this"}, {"start": 782.0, "end": 787.0, "text": "we have understood the second use case\nas well. This means we are done with all"}, {"start": 787.0, "end": 795.0, "text": "the use cases of scope resolution\noperator and this means we are done with"}, {"start": 795.0, "end": 801.0, "text": "the second topic as well.\nOkay friends, this is it for now. Thank"}, {"start": 801.0, "end": 806.0, "text": "you for watching this lecture. I will\nsee you in the next one."}, {"start": 806.0, "end": 811.0, "text": "[Applause]\n[Music]"}]'::jsonb, 'WEBVTT

