So, it is clear from this fact that, this data structure

47
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
is not a linear data structure.

48
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.000
We have another example, that is graph.

49
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Graph is also a non linear data structure.

50
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.000
After understanding the difference between

51
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.000
a linear data structure and 
a non linear data structure,

52
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
let''s even go further.

53
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000
We can make even further distinction.

54
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.000
We do have static data structures 
and dynamic data structures.

55
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Let''s discuss them one by one.

56
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.000
In these type of data structure,

57
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.000
the memory is allocated at compile time.

58
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
So, static data structures 
are those data structures

59
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.000
where the memory is allocated at compile time.

60
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Therefore, maximum size is fixed.

61
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.000
The advantage of such data structure is that,

62
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.000
we can access data very fast.

63
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.000
But on the other hand, disadvantage is that

64
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.000
insertion and deletion operations are slower.

65
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.000
We can take an example like this.

66
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Array data structure is a static data structure,

67
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.000
here you can see that, we 
have to fix the size beforehand.

68
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
That is why, we are fixing the size at

69
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.000
compilation time, that is when 
we are creating the code.

70
00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Maximum size is always fixed in the case of arrays.

71
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Advantage is obviously that, we 
can access the elements very fast,

72
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.000
but slower insertion and deletion.

73
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.000
We will discuss this, why 
this disadvantage is there

74
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.000
and why this advantage is there later.

75
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Right now, you should understand this point,

76
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000
that with static data structures we have

77
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
this advantage and this disadvantage.

78
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Now, let''s see what are dynamic data structures.

79
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.000
In these type of data structures,

80
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.000
the memory is allocated at run time.

81
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
Therefore, the maximum size is flexible.

82
00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.000
When the memory will be allocated at run time,

83
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.000
then user will decide the size.

84
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.000
In that case, the size is flexible. Okay.

85
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Advantage is of course, 
faster insertion and deletion.

86
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.000
But again the disadvantage is slower access.

87
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
So, we can clearly see that, there is nothing like

88
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.000
one data structure is better than the other.

89
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.000
The advantage of one is the 
disadvantage of the other.

90
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.000
So, choice of data structures 
purely depends upon the

91
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.000
user requirement. According to that, 
the data structure will get selected.

92
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.000
So, there is nothing like that, one data 
structure is better than the other. Okay.

93
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.000
And let me give you an example 
of a dynamic data structure.

94
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.000
You can see, the linked list is the best example

95
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.000
of a dynamic data structure.

96
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.000
We will discuss this later that 
how linked list can be created.

97
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.000
What are the advantages and disadvantages.

98
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.000
We will discuss all these in subsequent lectures.

99
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Okay friends, this is it for now.

100
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Thank you for watching this presentation.
'
