SELECT ivc.id, 'en', 'Hello everyone, welcome to Nesso Academy. In the previous lectures, we have understood the concept of classes and objects and we have also understood how to define member functions of a class. Now we are in this lecture and the name of this lecture is static data members. In this lecture we will properly understand what are static data members and how we can define them. So without any further delay, let''s get started with this lecture and let''s see what are the topics. The first topic is introduction to static data members. First I will introduce you to static data members. Then through an example we will understand how to declare, use and define a static data member. So these are the topics. Let''s start with the first one that is introduction to static data members. So what are static data members? A static data member is a member of the class that can be declared using the keyword static inside the class. So within the class we can only declare a static data member and we can declare the static data member with the help of the static keyword. If we want to define the static data member then we can only define it outside the class. This is what I have written as the second point. It must be defined outside the class also. it is shared by all the objects of the class. It is not the case that each object will receive its own copy of the static data member. Every object has to share the same copy of the static data member. So it is shared by all the objects of the class. Also if we want to access a static data member then it is possible through the class name not the object name. So it can be accessed using the class name because it is created on a class basis not on an object basis. It is not associated with an object. It is associated with the class. I hope these points are clear to you. Now let''s see how to declare a static data member inside the class. Let''s see the syntax for the same. This is the syntax we can follow to declare a static data member inside the class. We need to specify the keyword static. Then we need to provide the data type of the data member. And then after this we need to provide the variable name or the data member name. So in this way we can declare a static data member. Now what about its definition? How we can define a static data member outside the class? This is the syntax we can follow. First we need to specify the data type. Then after this the name of the class to which it belongs. After this with the help of scope resolution operator we can define our static data member. We need to provide the name of the static data member after the scope resolution operator. So this is how we can define a static data member. We can also initialize the static data member. At this moment we can use the list initialization or copy initialization or other forms of initialization. I hope this is clear to you. Now let''s see how to use a static data member. This is the usage of static data member. We need to specify the name of the class. Then after this the scope resolution operator and then the name of the static data member. Now here you can observe that we are using the scope resolution operator to define a static data member and to use the data member outside the class. This is the use case of the scope resolution operator. We already know that with the help of the scope resolution operator we can access global variables inside the function. Also with the help of scope resolution operator we can define member functions outside the class. In the same way we can define static data members outside the class with the help of scope resolution operator and this operator is also useful in accessing the static data member outside the class. I hope this is clear to you. Also I would like to mention that by default static data members are initialized to zero. So all static members are initialized to zero. If we do not provide any initialization value to the static data member then it will be initialized to zero by default. So these are the points about static data members. And now we know how to declare, define and use a static data member. We at this moment only know the syntax. Now let''s implement this. For this purpose, we need to move to the next topic. And through the example, we will learn how to declare, define, and use a static data member. For now, we are done with the introduction to static data members. Let''s move to the second topic to understand through an example how to declare, define and use static data members. Here is the example program. I have included IO stream header file and here is the definition of the class student. Within this class, I have declared this public keyword. This means the code following it is meant to be public. This means it is accessible to all the functions outside the class. Now here is the normal count variable and it is initialized to zero. This is the normal data member and therefore whenever we create an object of this class then the object will receive its own copy of this data member. This is what we need to remember and this is what we have already learned as well. After this I have defined this static data member as well. After this I have declared this static data member as well. I have followed the same syntax. First I have specified the data type as static int and then the name of the variable which is static count. This is just the declaration not the definition. Also we must remember this that this variable will be shared by all the objects of this class. Here is the definition of the static count variable. Here you can observe the same syntax being followed. First the data type is specified. Then the name of the class. Then after this the scope resolution operator and then the name of the static data member which is static count. and it is initialized to zero. Even though we do not initialize it to zero, it will be automatically initialized to zero. So now we know this static count variable has been defined and it is initialized to zero. After this we have this constructor called student. I''m calling this the constructor and we already know what a constructor is. I gave you the brief idea about what a constructor is. A constructor is a special type of function which gets called whenever the object of the class is created. So it will be called automatically when an object of this specific class will be created. Here we have this code and with the help of this code I am incrementing both normal count and static count by one. Now here is the definition of the main function. In this definition we have these three objects s_sub_1, s_sub_2 and s_sub_3 and these objects are of type student. So these are the objects of class student. As the object s1 is created, the constructor is called and normal count is incremented by one. We know that s1 has its own copy of this variable normal count. it will be incremented by one. Therefore, s1 dotn normal count is equal to one because it has been initialized to zero. Now it is equal to one. I hope this is clear to you. Now what about s_ub_2? Because s_ub_2 is also created. Constructor is called again and normal count is incremented by one. But s_ub_2 has its own copy of this normal count variable. It will be incremented by one. So s_ub_2 do.normal normal count is equal to 1. It has to do nothing with S1 dot normal count. S_ub_2 has its own copy of the normal count variable and it has updated normal count to one because of this constructor. Now what happens in case of S3 because this object is created constructor is called normal count is incremented. S3 dot normal count is also equal to one. So we know at this moment s_sub_1 dotn normal count is equal to 1. s_ub_2 dotnormal count is equal to 1 and s_sub_3 dotnormal count is also equal to 1. Now what happens in case of static count variable? What about this specific variable? We know s1 object is created. Therefore the constructor is called and static count variable is incremented by one. We also know this that static count variable does not belong to an object. The same copy of the static count variable will be shared by all the objects because of S1 static count will receive value one. This happens because of this line. I hope this is clear to you. So now static count variable has value one. What about s_ub_2? Because of s_ub_2 constructor is called. static count is incremented by one. Now it has value two. Please note that S2 does not have its own copy of static count variable. The same copy of static count variable is incremented and therefore we are getting value two inside this variable. I hope this is clear to you. The same thing happens for S3 as well. Again static count is incremented by one and we will get value three in this variable. So we now know that static count is equal to three. And with the help of these std see out statements I am trying to display the results of s_ub_1 dotn normal count, s_ub_2 dotn normal count, s3 dotnormal count and student static count. Here you can observe that I am using the syntax of accessing the static data member within this main function. First I am specifying the name of the class, then the scope resolution operator and then the name of the static data member. In this way we can access this static count variable. Now when we execute this program we will get the output s1.normal count equal 1, s_ub_2 dotnormal count equal to 1, s3 dotnormal count equal to 1 and shared static count equal to three. Here we can observe what we have expected. So from this example it is clear what is the difference between normal data member and static data member. Each object get its own copy of the normal data member. But each object has to share the same copy of the static data member. That is why we are seeing this output. So with this we are done with this example and this means we are done with the last topic as well and therefore we are done with this lecture. Okay friends this is it for now. Thank 