SELECT si.id, '# Study Guide: Static Data Members in C++

## Conceptual Overview
Video explains static data members in C++, covering declaration inside a class, definition outside the class, sharing across all objects, access via class name, scope resolution operator usage, default initialization to zero, and a practical example demonstrating differences from normal data members.

Static data members are declared with the static keyword inside a class
They are defined outside the class using the class name and scope resolution operator
All objects share a single copy of the static data member

## Key Terminology & Concepts
- **C++**: Foundational concept covered in this lecture.
- **Static Data Members**: Foundational concept covered in this lecture.
- **Class**: Foundational concept covered in this lecture.
- **Scope Resolution Operator**: Foundational concept covered in this lecture.
- **Oop**: Foundational concept covered in this lecture.

## Review Questions for Self-Assessment
1. What is the primary purpose and syntax of Static Data Members in C++?
2. How does the compiler or runtime handle edge cases for this construct?
3. In what scenarios should this pattern be used over alternative implementations?', 60
