SELECT ivc.id, 'en', 'Hello everyone, welcome to Nesso Academy. In the previous lecture, we understood friend classes. We got to know that we can define a class that can access private and protected members of some other class. We call that class the friend class of the other class. Now in this presentation, we will understand the concept of friend member functions. So without any further delay, let''s get started with this lecture and let''s see what are the topics. There is only one topic and the name of the topic is friend member functions. Now let''s understand what are friend member functions. A friend member function is a member function that can access private and protected members of some other class. First of all, it is a member function of some class. and it can access private and protected members of the other class. That is why it is called friend member function. Also, it is useful when we don''t want the entire class to have access. We know that when we define a friend class, then the entire class have access to the private and protected members of the other class. But what if we want that only the specific member functions of the class should be able to access private and protected members of the other class. If we want this then we should not define the class as friend class. Instead we can define some member functions the friend member functions. In this way, we will allow access to the private and protected members of the other class to some member functions only, not all the member functions of the class. I hope this idea is clear to you. Now to make this more clear, let''s take the same example program we took in the last lecture. Here is the example program we have understood in the last lecture. Here we have the class diary which mimics the real life diary that allows us to set the secret message via this function set secret. Through this function we can provide some string to this variable secret which is the private member of this class. Here